  "pretreatments": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "description": "Hollander beater pretreatment: A modified Hollander beater, model Reina, was used to comminute the algal biomass. The machine consists of an elliptic water raceway equipped with a bladed drum spinning at 580 RPM. The energy requirement of the machine's engine is 1 hp. A bed-plate with sharp grooves is located under the rotating wheel with dual functionality for cutting the material and decreasing the gap between blades and bed-plate. When the power is activated, blades and grooves exercise a cutting action while the high pressure and speed reached under the drum beat the mixture."
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "description": "Co-digestion with sludge: Digester sludge was used to inoculate batch digesters with the necessary microorganisms. A 25 L tank of sludge was collected from the anaerobic sludge vessels of the wastewater treatment plant of Celtic Anglian Water Ltd., Ringsend, Dublin. The sludge was used as substrate for anaerobic digestion purposes and it currently constitutes the main organic waste for biogas production in wastewater treatment facilities."
    }
  ]
}
