  "pretreatments": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "description": "Dilute citric acid pretreatment of sugarcane bagasse with temperature (T), time (t), and percentage by weight of citric acid (PCA) as operational variables, using a 2^3 Doehlert experimental design (DED) with five replicates at the center point (CP) and investigating conditions of 120 to 180 °C, 20 to 90 min, and 3 to 12 wt% PCA. The pretreatment was carried out in a pressurized system using a 316L-grade stainless steel tubular reactor (autoclave type) with 150 mL of aqueous citric acid solution, followed by cooling in an ice-water bath and pressing to separate the solid (SF) and liquid (BL) fractions. The solid fraction was characterized in terms of yield and chemical composition (cellulose, lignin, and hemicelluloses) and used in enzymatic hydrolysis. The liquid fraction was stored in hermetically sealed containers in a freezer."
    },
