    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "description": "Advanced oxidative pretreatment of sugarcane bagasse. The AOP was performed in a white acrylic cylindrical 2 L reactor equipped with a mechanical stirrer with a three-disc acrylic shaft with grooves, in order to improve the mass transfer during the pretreatment. In a typical run, the reactor vessel was loaded with 30 g (dry weight basis) of alkaline-extracted pretreated SB, followed by the addition of distilled water, an aqueous H_2O_2 solution, and drops of an aqueous 5 mol L^-1 NaOH solution, to give a defined LSR and to adjust the solution pH to 11.6. After the solution pH had been adjusted to 11.6, the suspension was stirred at 150 rpm and 25 °C for a defined time interval. During the AOP, a pH value of ~11.6 was maintained by adding drops of an aqueous 5 mol L^-1 NaOH solution. The composition of each reaction medium, in terms of applied H_2O_2 load and LSR, was obtained from the DED."
    }
  ]
}
